-- title:
--   Reading first-branch leading coefficients in the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a nonzero level $N$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$; fix modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality of the two Hecke maps $\bar\alpha,\bar\beta$ at level $(N,q)$, and a place specialization $P$ attached to these data. Let $R$ be a prolongation tuple over $P$, with $k$ perfect, let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $w$ be a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$ over $k$, and let $c$ be a system of node coordinates for $R$ over $K$ at $w$: elements $x,y$ of the ring $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K\,w$ of functions integral at both branches and at all places above $w$ and lying in the field over $K$, with first-branch residue of $x$ zero, second-branch residue of $x$ of order $1$ at the Frobenius translate of $w$, second-branch residue of $y$ zero, and first-branch residue of $y$ of order $1$ at $w$. Let $\varpi$ lie in $A \cap K$. Assume: the node ring is local and Noetherian with maximal ideal generated by the constant $\varpi$, $x$ and $y$ (`hmax`); every element of the node ring differs from some constant by a non-unit (`hres`); for $d \in A \cap K$ the restricted reduction of $d$ vanishes exactly when $\varpi \mid d$ (`h\varpi`); the value integrality law at $w$, i.e. for every $f$ integral at $w$'s branches and all places $V$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V = w$ one has $V.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$; and $w$ is a supersingular place (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set for $q$). Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, $\pi$ an irreducible element, $E \ge 1$, and let $\iota$ be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of the node ring at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \pi^E)$. Let $\mathrm{wmap} : A \cap K \to W$ send $\varpi$ to $\pi$, let $\iota$ carry constants to the corresponding constants of the crossing model, and let $\rho : W \to k$ be compatible with the restricted reduction on $A \cap K$. Assume further that some place $V_0$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ satisfies $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V_0 = w$, and the value–residue compatibility `hVAL`: for every $g$ in the node ring and every place $V$ above $w$, the first-branch residue of $g$ has value $\mathrm{red}(V.\mathrm{evalAt}\,g)$ at $w$. Let $\beta_V, \alpha_U$ be units of the crossing model with $\iota(\hat y) = V\beta_V$ and $\iota(\hat x) = U\alpha_U$, and let $G_\beta \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ represent $\beta_V$. Finally let $f$ be in the node ring with nonzero first-branch residue of order $n \in \mathbb{N}$ at $w$, and let $\gamma$ be a unit with $\iota(\hat f) - \gamma V^n$ in the ideal generated by the constant $\pi$ and by $U$, represented by $G_\gamma \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$. The conclusion is that the function $(\text{first-branch residue of } f)/(\text{first-branch residue of } y)^n$ lies in the valuation subring of $w$ and its residue there is the image of $\rho(G_\gamma(0)) \cdot \rho(G_\beta(0))^{-n}$.
--
--   This is the local reading, in the $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E)$ model of a supersingular crossing on the special fibre, of the leading coefficient of a function along the first branch: the value at $w$ of the normalised ratio is computed from the constant terms of representatives of the two units $\gamma$ and $\beta_V$. It is used in the construction of the values of the first- and second-branch ratios and their comparison with the angular factor at an inertia-stable node.
